      },
      "displayName": "Aaron Birkland",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2745"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2745",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " suggests that Fedora MUST create (at least paths for) ACLs for all resources, so presumably that would encompass the LDP-RS and the NonRDFSource.  ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2744"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2744",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " suggests revisiting the need for acl:accessControl in the first place, so \"triple in their metadata\" might not be the relevant factor to consider.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
