     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2745\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2745</a> suggests that Fedora MUST create (at least paths for) ACLs for all resources, so presumably that would encompass the LDP-RS and the NonRDFSource.  </p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2744\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://jira.duraspace.org/browse/FCREPO-2744</a> suggests revisiting the need for acl:accessControl in the first place, so \"triple in their metadata\" might not be the relevant factor to consider.</p>",
